A||N||3||FieroKohl||Erratic idling on cold start-'88 GT||||1||
Z||000000||FieroKohl||10-15-2001||09:30 PM||||I'm having major cold start problems.  On a cold start (no problem warm) my RPM's are erratic. (It does stall sometimes on start up).  I start it up and the needle jumps close to 2 then zooms all the way down to almost zero and it sounds like it's going to die on me, then jumps all the way back up near 2 and does this for about a whole minute or so.  Yes, I'm NOT exagerrating.  It does it for that long...like it doesn't know what to do.  Then it calms down slowly to around 1.5 and I just wait patiently for 4-5 minutes until it completely calms down to 1.  If I don't do that then I drive with it all shaky until it calms down on it's own.<BR>This is ridiculous.  I have been to two Fiero shops and they have tried everything in the book.  I notice that when I fill it up with gas then start the car it does the RPM jumping thing real quick then settles down.  sometimes I have to give it a little gas to calm it down further.  Then when I'm out driving awhile and park it, I putit into park and RPM needle does a little jumping thing up to close to 2 then comes right back down and I turn off the engine.  <P>We've hooked up the scanner to read codes but everything looks fine.  <P>I do notice that my fuel mileage is really bad.  It's using too much fuel for some reason.  I notice a lil' hiccupping when I'm driving at a steady pace but it's hardly noticeable.  I'm coming up on my Smog check and I know with this problem I'm not going to pass.<P>A little background:  I'm the original owner.  It's in perfect condition otherwise.  Just had a 3.4 engine put in but the problem persists so it has nothing to do with an engine problem.  I live in Southern California so the cold start problem isn't cuz it's really cold.  This had been a problem for almost a year and has gotten worse in the last month or two.  I have 171,000 miles on it.  <P>Any suggestions?  Any comments will be appreciated.<P>Thank you,<P>Kohl (I'm a girl...I know it's hard to tell with a name like that)<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||ka4nkf||10-15-2001||10:29 PM||||First of all Welcome to the Forum.<BR>With that many miles I would change the MAT sensor in the air filter canister. If that does not help then change the ECM temp sensor located below the thermostat housing (pointing Horiz)||||reg||1
Z||000002||Indiana_resto_guy||10-15-2001||11:21 PM||||Don't rule out vacuum leaks. The erratic idle is one thing when cold. The poor mileage can be another. If you find some, the O2 sensor can be bad now as well.<BR>Welcome and good luck!||||reg||1
Z||000003||AL||10-15-2001||11:25 PM||||hi,i see the problem persists,didn't they say it was the cold start injector? how long has this been going on? since you put in the new engine or a little time after that? sooner or latter you'll figure it out,glad you found us, do you still want the rail? i can send you a pic if you want,then you we can negotiate a price,welcome again and it was nice meeting you.<B>AL</B> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/AL_sig.gif">  <P>------------------<BR> ||||reg||1
